#. Tag: title
#: intro-pluginsupport.docbook:1
#, no-c-format
msgid "Supported Plugins"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: intro-pluginsupport.docbook:3
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"One of the nicest things about &digikam; is how easily its functionality can "
"be extended, by using <emphasis>plugins</emphasis>. The <ulink url=\"https://"
"quickgit.kde.org/?p=kipi-plugins.git\">Kipi project</ulink> is dedicated to "
"develop a plugin interface for &digikam;. Plugins setup is described in this "
"<link linkend=\"using-setup-plugins\">section</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: intro-pluginsupport.docbook:10
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &digikam; plugins interface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: intro-pluginsupport.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Plugins are dedicated mostly to export and import images with remote web "
"services. Their advantage is, that it is much easier to add a capability to "
"&digikam; by writing a small plugin than by modifying the &digikam; core."
msgstr ""

#~ msgid "Color Management"
#~ msgstr "Xestión de color"
